// CROWN — a held resume runs its remainder INSIDE the frame that calls it.
// `apply` declares `!Log` and calls its callback; the callback resumes a held
// continuation (the arm computes after `apply` returns, so the op is
// multi-shot and `resume` calls the record), and the remainder `□ + note(2)`
// performs Log inside apply's extent. The resume charged nothing, so the
// callback's row was Pure and apply's gate had nothing to judge: accepted by
// boot 477bb667, ran to 3. The resume performs its world now — the handler's
// remainder-world cell, gated by apply through the callback's row — and the
// install judges that gate against its own remainder. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
effect Cell { bump() -> Int }
effect Log { note(x: Int) -> Int }
fn apply(f) with !Log = f() + 0
handler cell { bump() => apply(() => resume(1)) }
handler log { note(x) => resume(x) }
fn body() = bump() + note(2)
fn main() = ({ body() } ~> cell) ~> log
